<font face="Arial" size="+1"><B>Ultima Online 2 - UO2 Vault Chat for 1/10/2001</B></font>
		<p></p>

<font face=arial size=-1><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> Welcome to tonight's chat with the Dev Team of Origin
<br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> Tonight, Big_D, ColinRae, Drax and Ghosty will be taking questions
<br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> To send a question to them, just type "/msg name question" so if you would like to send something to Drax 

for instance
<br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> Just type "/msg Drax your question here"
<br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> Go ahead and start submitting your questions and Cynthe has something to say in the meantime
<br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> Take it away Cynthe
<br><b>&lt;Cynthe&gt;</b> Hey everyone... it's great that you could come! Every time one of these rolls around I feel like a few of 

you are more familiar. :)    There's no specific topic tonight, but some of our leads are around, and if they can 

answer a question, they will.  Bear in mind, though, that if we're not absolutely certain how something will work 

just yet, we don't talk about it... that way, there's less misinformation and disappointment later.
<br><b>&lt;Cynthe&gt;</b> I know this all sounds familar... :)
<br><b>&lt;Cynthe&gt;</b> But is your question doesn't get answered, understand that we'd rather say nothing on a subject than say 

something that might be wrong
<br><b>&lt;Cynthe&gt;</b> Okay?
<br><b>&lt;Cynthe&gt;</b> Cool!
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Woot!
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> *Sanctum-Shadex* What kinds of spells can we expect in the Ether tree besides the ambiguous "goodie goodie 

magic"?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Ether magic is more than just 'goodie goodie' magic.  
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Ether mages are over-mages, they are about the magic of magic, and their spell effects are powerful and 

overwhelming
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> but they tend to not allow for frequent casts, due to that power.
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> Ether isn't just warm and fuzzy magic. :)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> They do stand as opposites to Necromancy, though.  The two schools are opposite 'master schools', designed 

for the most powerful of all mages.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> &lt;Balefire&gt; Hey everyone, a question about leaping attacks...If a monster is running by and I do a leap 

attack, will I end up jumping behind the monster, or am I locked onto it and I'll follow it?
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> For the leaping attacks it will depend if you annoy the monster enough. 
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> If you do manage to hit him and damage him he will turn to attack you.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Bale, if you mean that in the sense of "will I miss moving critters with leap attacks" the answer is, 

there's a chance it'll look funny (though we try to stop most cases) but in general you'll still be able to hit the 

monster.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> &lt;Ar-Kane&gt; For those who like 1st view..Can we still have any hope for Origin?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Hope, yes, but one thing to consider is that games work best when you focus on making one preferable to the 

other.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> FOr example, EQ is more fun to play first person (as is quake and unreal), and AC is more suited for 3rd 

person (as is Heretic II)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> As a result, we've made several design decisions based on the fact that the majority of people will be in 3rd 

person.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> For example, can you imagine doing a flying jump triple flip kick in first person?  What would happen?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Other than you throwing the hell up, of course.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Other things, such as dancing, also is a lot less fun in 1st person.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> As a result, we're concentrating on 3rd person.  There is always the chance that 1st person will come later
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> But even if it does, it's not a short-term priority, and the game probably won't seem as optimal to that 

viewpoint.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> On the bright side, you can move the camera where you want, as long as it's centered on the person
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> SO people who prefer a more top-down view could concievably play like that.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Although it won't be like UO - the camera will turn with your character.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> *Zax* Are Assassins going to have special certain death attacks? Or are they just going to be just another 

fighter but with a rouge title?
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> Each of the combat specializations will have unique attacks.
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> As Gaffer has pointed out we will balance these with each other so forming groups makes strategic 

sense.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> No insta-death is a pretty good thought tho :)
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> You will want to have heavy weapon users to stun folks so the assasin types can dart in with thier 

stabs.
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> Yeah good point Gaffer, don't expect any insta-death type skills or spells. Exploit city.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> *Grim* how big will the groups be, and will there be a way to chat with your group?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> We'll be honest, we haven't decided yet.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Currently our parties max out at 8, but we could make that bigger (or smaller!)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> There are some benefits to larger groups, of course, but there's also an optimum size for a group that we 

will want to nudge people towards.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> We'll know more about that as we fiddle more with actual play testing.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> You guys are free to voice your opinion on the subject on the boards.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> &lt;FireKnight&gt; question. Since camera will be static to your back, can you make your character transparent, 

like 50%, so you could see in front of him? It would be very useful in closed areas and sometimes when you're 

running and jumping.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> FireKnight:  No, sorry.  (Why?  Because of the intricacies of how our character stitching/clothing/hueing 

system works on some cards, making things transparent that are also all that other stuff would look really bad on 

some cards.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> But as cards get better, we can re examine that.  I've liked that effect in some games that did it well.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> *Grim* will you be able to engage multiple targets with special attacks? ala a whirlwind attack or 

something similar?
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> We actually do have some combat strokes that do area effects
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> However since those are very powerful they will require high skills and won't be useable as often as 

single target moves.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> *Gonj* Will Origin include "rares" as a money sink like in UO?
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> The treasure system has the ability to generate one in a million items...
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> So those could technically be considered rares....
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> Also, the creation of certain items may require some tighty controlled rare substances...
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> that cost a bundle to get a hold of...
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> So in a sense, I guess we do have some of that.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> &lt;OrionStratics&gt; With the magic system almost complete, can you finally give us some examples of spells and 

their effects?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Certainly.  The four primary schools each have their own personality to them, and thus have spells that suit 

them well.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> For example, fire concentrates on damage, water on healing, earth on enchantments (buffs) and air is more 

general purpose.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Each of the schools also have spells designed to help out each other
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> For example, fire mages have spells that can make earth mages more powerful.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> And each of the schools also have spells designed to defend against or hose another school
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> FOr example, water magic happens to have some surprises for those uppity fire mages.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Expect some rare-cast spells (i.e. spells you can only use once an hour, once a day, or rarer!)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> And expect a lot of spells that reinforce the notion of the party
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Some of the spells are designed to, for example, make monsters more vulnerable to warrior attacks.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> of course, that's just the tip of the iceberg
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> *Azriel* What will be your policy on screenshots taken by early beta players? Will they have to send them 

through someone at the team, who will post the ones they deem postable?
<br><b>&lt;Cynthe&gt;</b> I'm not sure exactly how that will work, but as far as the community goes, once the game hits beta, it's 

practically live, since there will be people talking about it, and lots of people will be seeing it.  So we'll be 

beginning our screenshot of the week, etc. at that point.  So to answer your question, yes... they should be sent 

in, and we'll approve shots for posting on our site, much in the same way that UO does.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> *Arthur_Pendragon* Will we all be starting on the exact same continent (Britannia) or will we be on the 

continent matching our race?
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> There are three starting areas that are all safe zones. 
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> The largest is Britannia but there is also an island that has a Meer Colony and an island with a Juka 

colony.
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> This allows folks to start off in a 'native culture' if they wish while still be protected by the safe 

zone when they start.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> *Grim* will the timers on the rare-cast spells refresh while you are offline or must you be logged on for 

