<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Earth and Air.
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> Isn't it obvious? :)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Water and Earth is Nature.
<br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b>  *Mitt* Question: Will you implement factions to the game? So that Necromancers for example will not get 

attacked by the undeads?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Our AI tracks who it likes and dislikes in a different fashion from a pure 'faction' system like EQ's
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Monsters track things and people that it likes, trusts, hates and fears, and that dictates it's behavior.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Including things like them ignoring players it doesn't have problems with, or coming to the aid of other 

monsters in need of assistance.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> We've had one guy (you've seen him on the boards as Thor a couple times) doing almost exclusively AI for the 

last few months
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> SO I think you guys will be pleased with the results of it.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> *EthanWard* Blackthorn, will you be playing Blackthorn in the game?
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> As much as I can until they pull me off onto whatever comes next. I love interacting with the players 

when I can.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> (he plays Blackthorn in the office sometimes too)
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> (the horrid torturing part though mostly)
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> Some old schoolers out there might remember me answering GM calls during beta of UO and in the early 

days.
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> There were some surprised fans out there when I showed up to help them out. Of course there were my 

infamous wrestling matches that no one can forget (try as they might).
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> &lt;Banstyle&gt; Will the ability to jump and duck be commands, like keyboard commands? Will we be able to use 

them in a non-combat fashion? Will there be various places in the world that require actions like these to be 

accessible?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> I've blocked those out
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Yes, you can jump.  Ducking - not currently.  
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> You can use them in non-combat places.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> However, we've made a conscious decision to avoid making places where jumping and ducking are really 

necessary
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> To be honest, I've usually found jumping puzzles to be a game design copout more often than not, so unless it 

is an extremely natural fit for the locale at hand, don't expect to see any of 'em.
<br><br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> We're going to wrap up the chat now, I'd like to thank everyone for coming tonight and I'd like to thank 

the Dev Team for coming out to talk with us
<br><b>&lt;Cynthe&gt;</b> Thanks to everyone for coming!!  It's been great... and we really do look forward to seeing more from you 

on our boards and the other boards around the community.  For those who don't have a UO account and would like more 

interaction with the team, don't forget there's a UWOO eGroup created, and lots of us are on it.  We don't answer 

much necessarily, but it's a good option for those who want to know they're heard but don't have UO accounts to post 

on our 
<br><b>&lt;Blackthorn&gt;</b> Thanks everyone for coming! Great to talk to you all!
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> See ya, all
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Thanks again to come and listen to us ramble.  
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Thanks so much, uo2vault!
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> And good Q's tonight fans...
<br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> We'll have a log up soon of the chat over on the UO2 Vault, thanks again!
<br><b>&lt;Gasper&gt;</b> We now return you to your regularly scheduled program already in progress


</font>

</td></tr></table>

